3. should calculate base premium as 60 G for an amulet\n4. should calculate base premium as 80 G for a staff\n5. should calculate base premium as 40 G for a potion\n6. should calculate base premium as 25 G per component (rune or moonstone)\n7. should apply special base premium of 60 G for exactly 3 alike components (e.g., 3 runes)\n8. should not apply block when there are 2 runes and 1 moonstone - different types\n9. should apply two separate blocks for 3 runes and 3 moonstones\n10. should not apply block for 4 runes - block requires exactly 3\n11. should calculate 175 G base premium for 7 runes\n12. should add 50% risk surcharge for cursed items (applies only to the item's base)\n13. should add 30% risk surcharge for highly enchanted items (enchantment level ≥ 5)\n14. should apply 20% loyalty discount for customers with ≥ 2 years with MHPCO\n15. should add 10% initial assessment surcharge for first insurance (per item)\n16. should apply 15% discount for each contract after the first\n17. should add 5 G processing fee to every premium\n18. should round final premium up to whole G in MHPCO's favor (e.g., 197.5 → 198)\n19. should round final payout down to whole G in MHPCO's favor (e.g., 350.5 → 350)\n20. should calculate 165 G premium for a newcomer with a cursed sword: (100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance) + 5 fee = 165\n21. should calculate 160 G premium for a long-standing customer's second contract with a cursed highly-enchanted sword: (100 + 50 + 30 - 20 - 15 = 145) + 5 = 150\n22. should apply 100 G deductible per damage event\n23. should apply 100 G deductible per damaged item in multi-item damage\n24. should cap total payout per policy at twice the insurance sum\n25. should calculate insurance sum correctly for a policy with sword and amulet as 1600 G\n26. should calculate cap as 2000 G for a sword (1000 G value)\n27. should calculate insurance sum as 1750 G for a sword and 3 runes, cap as 3500 G\n28. should reduce payout to remaining cap when cap is exhausted\n29. should reimburse 50% of damage for items with enchantment level ≥ 8\n30. should fully reimburse damage for items made of dragon material\n31. should apply 50% rule instead of dragon material when both apply (e.g., dragon sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 → payout 400)\n32. should fully reimburse dragon-material sword with enchantment 5, damage 800 → payout 700\n33. should reimburse 50% for steel sword with enchantment 9, damage 1000 → payout 400\n34. should calculate 400 G payout for regular sword (steel, enchantment 3), damage 500 G\n35. should calculate 100 G payout for damage to a rune (insurance 250 G), damage 200 G\n36. should handle error cases: unknown item type, claim on unowned item, negative"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"nebius/qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784950465606,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-55975c49-1a16-4b5b-ae5c-01e6cbff117d","responseModel":"Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507"}}
